# P-locks: on EDIT, hold a step that is on and turn a sound knob: that step gets its own value (one
# step of the knob's lane); a tap still toggles. SAVE + the knob, holding the step, clears it.
wait 300
expect view 1
expect part 0
expect sound0.0.0 34
# the 909 kick on steps 1 and 5 (taps on empty steps: on at once)
tapkey w0
tapkey w4
expect hit0.0.0 1
expect hit0.0.4 1
# hold step 5 (on already), turn KNOB 1 (TUNE): step 5's own tune; the knob's own stays
key w4 down
spin K1 20
key w4 up
expect hit0.0.4 1
expect sound0.0.0 34
expect lanes 1
expect laneval0.0.0.4 54
expect laneval0.0.0.0 255
# held without a knob: the step stays; a tap takes it off, and back on
key w0 down
wait 600
key w0 up
expect hit0.0.0 1
tapkey w0
expect hit0.0.0 0
tapkey w0
expect hit0.0.0 1
# playing: step 5 is heard with its tune, step 1 with the knob's
tap PLAY
wait 450
expect playhead0 5
expect motion0.0.0 54
wait 160
expect playhead0 6
expect motion0.0.0 34
tap PLAY
# SAVE + the knob, holding the step: the lock goes (the lane with it)
key w4 down
press SAVE
spin K1 1
release SAVE
key w4 up
expect lanes 0
expect hit0.0.4 1
# SEQ: holding a drum step and turning a knob locks nothing
tap SEQ
key w4 down
spin K1 5
key w4 up
expect lanes 0
# the 303 on EDIT: a held step's CUTOFF; on SEQ its NOTE, as before
turn ALGO 2
tap EDIT
tapkey w2
key w2 down
spin K1 -20
key w2 up
expect laneval2.0.0.2 28
expect sound2.0.0 48
tap SEQ
key w2 down
turn K1 2
key w2 up
expect lanes 1
